<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_RainbowPigment.xml                 UtinniPatches · COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1
  ============================================================================
  Harvest of `RUT_WelcomeBlanket` (ThingDefs_Plants/, same pass). the_scald.md
  §7 "Uniquely available — Rainbow pigment: mat-harvest dyes; the artistic
  economy's raw color (sibling to the Miasma's attar: one restores beauty,
  one supplies it)." No Miasma "attar" ThingDef exists yet to pattern-match
  against (checked; sibling in name only, not in an already-built def this
  pass can copy).

  Plain resource good, same shape as this mod's own `RUT_WickStem.xml`
  precedent (harvest of a wild-forage plant, no comps): nothing about a
  dye/pigment resource item needs a comp of its own; whatever eventually
  consumes it (an art-economy recipe, a trade good) reads it by defName,
  not by any comp here.

  MarketValue 3.0 is an explicit INVENTED PLACEHOLDER — a pigment/dye good
  priced above a plain fuel-stock item like WickStem's 1.5 (rarer, harder
  to reach: the Scald's margins are a "cool enough to drink" ring that
  still sits inside the hottest crater on the planet), not a real economy
  call; "items pass owns pricing" per this mod's own stated practice.

  🔴 Texture: a first draft reused vanilla Chemfuel's texPath as a bottled-
  liquid-dye placeholder, same posture as `RUT_WelcomeBlanket.xml` — but
  `validate_patch.py` refused it as a hard ERROR, the exact trap
  `RUT_Tarred_Solvents.xml`'s own header already documents in this same
  mod: UtinniPatches already ships its OWN art under
  Textures/Things/Item/Resource/ (RUT_Greenwood.png, RUT_Bitumen/, etc.), so
  that folder is this mod's claimed namespace and nothing outside it (not
  even a real vanilla texPath, which is AssetBundle-packed and has no loose
  file to find besides) is consulted. Repointed to a new RUT_-named folder
  (`Textures/Things/Item/Resource/RUT_RainbowPigment/RUT_RainbowPigment.png`,
  Graphic_StackCount is a Graphic_Collection subclass — texPath is a FOLDER)
  with a simple procedurally-drawn placeholder jar-with-rainbow-bands icon
  (64x64 RGBA, PIL-generated this pass), same posture as
  `RUT_Tarred_Solvents.xml`'s own placeholder chunk icons. Real (hand-
  authored, reviewed) art is still owed — see `RUT_WelcomeBlanket.xml`'s own
  header for the queued artpipe job covering both this item and its source
  plant.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_RainbowPigment</defName>
    <label>rainbow pigment</label>
    <description>A jar of thick, vividly banded dye rendered down from welcome-blanket mats. Each batch carries whatever hue the water was when the mat that made it grew — no two jars ever quite match, and dyers prize that as much as the color itself.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_RainbowPigment</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>3.0</MarketValue>
      <MaxHitPoints>50</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>0.05</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>2.0</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
